# Where the backend is.
#
# FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT this is optional. `npm run dev` falls back to
# http://localhost:8000 on its own, so you do not need a .env file at all
# unless your backend runs somewhere else.
#
# FOR A PRODUCTION BUILD it is REQUIRED. The build itself still succeeds, but
# the deployed page stops immediately with a clear message in the browser
# console saying this variable is missing.
#
# That is on purpose. The old behaviour fell back to "localhost", which in a
# deployed site means the VISITOR'S own computer -- so the page loaded
# perfectly and nothing worked, with no hint why. A page that names its own
# cause is much easier to fix.
#
# Set it to the backend's real address, with no trailing slash:
#
#     VITE_API_URL=https://insta-clone-api.onrender.com
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite substitutes this value when you BUILD, not when the page
# runs. Changing it later means rebuilding, not restarting.
#
# WARNING: every VITE_ variable is baked into the JavaScript sent to every
# visitor, so treat all of them as PUBLIC. An address is fine here. A password,
# a database URL or a secret key never is -- those belong in backend/.env only.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
